        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lansingnc.us/history-lansing",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 1930s and 1940s, Lansing housed one of Ashe County’s only cheese factories, giving local farmers a nearby processing plant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lansing%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s single stop sign sits at the lone three‑way intersection of NC 194 and Big Horse Creek Road, the only traffic control in Lansing.",
